; console_record.n64 - THE CONSOLE RECORD of the playable cart (design note, step N9).
;
; WHAT IT KEEPS: what the console cart is built to tell while the game is played - frames shown and not shown, sound
; underruns, the frame time in Count ticks (46.875 MHz; the whole period from one guest frame's end to the next, and
; the emulator's own work in it: the period less the time slept waiting for a free picture buffer, NesShowGetFb),
; the worst and the mean of each and a histogram in 1 ms steps; the RSP's clocks a frame as its program reports them
; (the status word +8 of each frame's area, summed by show.n64 in NesShowStat 12 / 13); the RDP's four counters
; (DPC CLOCK, BUFBUSY, PIPEBUSY, TMEM, 24 bits at the RCP clock, read straight from the RDP once a guest frame - the
; library has no call for them); the show's own counts (waits, drains, fallback lines, bands); the controller seen;
; and why the emulator stopped, if it did.
;
; WHERE: the flash cart's SDRAM (a SummerCart64), which the coordinator dumps over USB after the run, the console
; off: SDRAM 0x01600000 - 0x016F0FFF (KSEG1 $B1600000; 0xF1000 bytes) for the playable cart, and for the cart that
; hashes every picture (#NES_REC_PICTURES_ALL, the scrolling test cart) 0x01800000 - 0x019D0FFF (KSEG1 $B1800000;
; 0x1D1000 bytes) - the two never overlap, and no other cart of the project uses either. The cart asks the SC64
; once, at start, to allow writes to its ROM space (as the tile probe and the hardware carts do: NesRecScEnable); the
; record is kept only if its header reads back, and the side bands say so (show.n64: green kept, yellow not).
;   +$0000   the header, 16 words: "NESC", the ROM's CRC (the cartridge's word at $10), the version, the power-ons
;            seen, the run slot this power-on writes, #NES_REC_HASH_MAX, #NES_REC_HASH_EVERY (version 5)
;   +$1000   run slot k (k = power-on - 1 mod 8) at +$1000 + k x #NES_REC_SLOT ($1E000; all pictures: $3A000):
;            +0      the summary, #NES_REC_WORDS words (the #R_ list below); "NRUN" in word 0 once it is valid
;            +$1000  the series: one entry of 4 words for every 60 guest frames (about a second), up to 4,096
;                    (68 minutes): shown | not shown << 8 | underruns << 16 | frames with a button held << 24;
;                    the worst period; the worst work; the RSP's clocks in those 60 frames
;            +$11000 the events (NesRecEvent): 512 entries of 18 words - the first 256 kept, then a ring of the
;                    latest 256 - one for every guest frame with a sound underrun, a picture skipped, a drain, or
;                    work over one NES frame (779,970 ticks); the #E_ list below says what each holds
;            +$1A000 the picture hashes (NesRecPicture): #NES_REC_HASH_MAX entries (512; all pictures: 4,096) of
;                    8 words - frame, the hash of NES columns 0-239 (lo, hi), the hash of columns 240-255 (lo, hi),
;                    the frame's fallback lines, 0, 0
;   The record's tools decode it (console_record.py beside the cart). Version 3 (2026-11-26): the events grew from
;   8 words to 16 - the frame's work split into its parts (#E_TBAND on) - the summary keeps the same split summed
;   over the run (#R_T); the run slot grew from $15000 to $19000. Version 4 (the same day): the picture hashes; the
;   run slot $1D000, the whole area $E9000 bytes. Version 5 (the same day, with the APU split): the APU's parts are
;   the timing in the hot unit (its calls, of them the segment path, its ticks) and the synthesis by block (its
;   ticks); events of 18 words (+ the synthesis, + what is left: the guest CPU, the PPU and the bus); the hash count
;   per build; the run slot $1E000 ($3A000 with every picture hashed). Version 6 (N10, the synthesis on the RSP):
;   the synthesis column (#T_SYN) is its CPU side (rspsyn.n64's job polls); the summary's words 214-218 hold the
;   RSP's side - its jobs' clocks (DPC_CLOCK, 64 bits), jobs, renders for room, samples rendered. The layout is
;   version 5's otherwise.
;
; THE PICTURE HASHES (version 4; every shown picture in the build #NES_REC_PICTURES_ALL, which needs no input). The owner plays freely, so the picture cannot be checked against a reference while
; he plays; but from the power-on until the first button the guest runs exactly as the emulator's run of the same
; cart with no input does (the title and its demo), so every shown frame whose number is a multiple of
; #NES_REC_HASH_EVERY in that stretch is hashed - the NES picture's 256 x 240 pixels as the console's RDP drew them,
; read back from the buffer after its SYNC_FULL, in two parts: columns 0-239 and the rightmost 16 (240-255) - and the
; decoder compares them with the emulator's: the first frame that differs, and on which side. Hashing stops for good
; at the first button seen. A hash costs ~3-4 ms (the buffer's 7,680 lines invalidated and read), one frame in four,
; only before the game is touched.
;
; THE WORK SPLIT (version 3): Count ticks spent, per frame, in each part of the emulator that is not the guest's own
; instructions - accumulated where each part runs (NesRecT, show.n64; the unit calls timed copies of the three
; renderer routines it calls on a fallback line; unit/apu.n64 times the APU timing and counts its calls,
; unit/apu_cold.n64 its segment path and the DMC bytes, apusynth.n64 times the synthesis, mmc3_ppu_bus.n64 counts the
; PPU writes), all only in this build. What is left of the frame's work is the guest CPU, the PPU state machine and the
; bus. Each timed part includes the cache misses it takes itself, not those it leaves the code after it to take.
;
; HOW IT STAYS OUT OF THE GAME'S WAY: everything is counted in RAM once a guest frame (NesRecFrame, called from
; NesHostGuestFrame - compiled code at the frame's wrap, outside the hot unit); once every 60 guest frames the summary
; words that changed and the window's 4 series words go out, a PI write each (LpmDebugIoWrite), a few dozen at most.
; Nothing here is read by the emulator, so the guest runs the same with or without the record.
;
; A RUN THAT ENDS: the owner switching off loses at most the last 60 frames' counts. The emulator stopping (NES STOP)
; writes state 3 with the stop's reason and the whole summary at once (NesRecStop), then the screen turns red.

CompilerIf #NES_REC_PICTURES_ALL
  ; the cart that runs by itself (the scrolling test): every shown picture hashed, buttons or not
  #NES_REC = $B1800000                  ; KSEG1: cartridge $11800000 = SDRAM 0x01800000
  #NES_REC_HASH_MAX = 4096              ; entries of 32 bytes (68 s of pictures)
  #NES_REC_HASH_EVERY = 1               ; every shown frame
  #NES_REC_HASH_PADSTOP = 0             ; a button does not stop the hashing
CompilerElse
  #NES_REC = $B1600000                  ; KSEG1: cartridge $11600000 = SDRAM 0x01600000
  #NES_REC_HASH_MAX = 512
  #NES_REC_HASH_EVERY = 4               ; a shown frame whose number is a multiple of this is hashed
  #NES_REC_HASH_PADSTOP = 1             ; until the first button
CompilerEndIf
#NES_REC_MAGIC = $4E455343              ; "NESC"
#NES_REC_RUN_MAGIC = $4E52554E          ; "NRUN"
#NES_REC_VERSION = 6
#NES_REC_SLOTS = 8
#NES_REC_HASHES = $1A000                ; the picture hashes (NesRecPicture), from the slot's start
#NES_REC_SLOT = #NES_REC_HASHES + #NES_REC_HASH_MAX * 32   ; summary 4 KB + series 64 KB + events 36 KB + pictures
#NES_REC_EVENTS = $11000                ; the events, from the slot's start
#NES_REC_EVENT_MAX = 512                ; entries of 72 bytes: 0-255 the first, 256-511 a ring of the latest
#NES_REC_EVENT_WORDS = 18
#NES_REC_SLOW = 779970                  ; one NES frame in Count ticks (46.875 MHz / 60.0988 Hz): work over it is an event
#NES_REC_SERIES = $1000                 ; the series, from the slot's start
#NES_REC_SERIES_MAX = 4096              ; entries of 16 bytes
#NES_REC_WORDS = 224
#NES_REC_WINDOW = 60                    ; guest frames an entry
#NES_REC_MS = 46875                     ; Count ticks a millisecond
; the summary's words
#R_MAGIC = 0
#R_BOOT = 1
#R_STATE = 2                            ; 1 started, 2 running (a guest frame seen), 3 the emulator stopped, 4 did not start
#R_CODE = 3                             ; state 3: the bad opcode (0 none); state 4: 2 the cartridge, 3 the show's set-up
#R_PC = 4                               ; state 3: the 6502's PC
#R_WORKER = 5                           ; state 3: WorkerError
#R_FRAMES = 6                           ; guest frames run
#R_SHOWN = 7                            ; pictures shown (NesShowStat 0)
#R_NOTWORDS = 8                         ; not shown: the frame's words or fallback rows did not fit (1)
#R_NOTSOUND = 9                         ; not shown: the sound reserve ran low, the picture was skipped (14)
#R_OVER = 10                            ; shown after a drain (2)
#R_STARVE = 11                          ; sound underruns: the AI ran empty (HostAiStarvations)
#R_STARVELAST = 12                      ; the guest frame of the last
#R_DROPPED = 13                         ; sound samples dropped (HostAudioDropped)
#R_PSUM = 14                            ; the frame period, Count ticks: sum (lo, hi), max, the frame of the max
#R_PMAX = 16
#R_PMAXF = 17
#R_WSUM = 18                            ; the work (the period less the sleep for a buffer): sum (lo, hi), max, its frame
#R_WMAX = 20
#R_WMAXF = 21
#R_MEASURED = 22                        ; periods measured (the frames after the first)
#R_RSPSUM = 23                          ; the RSP's clocks: sum (lo, hi), the most in a frame
#R_RSPMAX = 25
#R_DPC = 26                             ; the RDP's counters, sums (lo, hi): CLOCK 26, BUFBUSY 28, PIPEBUSY 30, TMEM 32
#R_PIPEMAX = 34                         ; PIPEBUSY: the most in a guest frame
#R_WAITS = 35                           ; show.n64's counts: waits for a record or a row (3), drains (4), fallback lines (5),
#R_DRAINS = 36                          ; the most in a frame (6), split lines (7), lost bands (8), bands (10), the most
#R_FBLINES = 37                         ; Count ticks a band's close took (11)
#R_FBMOST = 38
#R_SPLIT = 39
#R_LOST = 40
#R_BANDS = 41
#R_BANDMAX = 42
#R_HELD = 43                            ; guest frames with a button held, pad 1 or 2
#R_PADS = 44                            ; the last buttons: pad 1 | pad 2 << 8 (NES order: A B Select Start Up Down Left Right)
#R_ENTRIES = 45                         ; series entries written
#R_UPDATES = 46                         ; times the summary went out
#R_SLEEP = 49                          ; Count ticks slept for a buffer, all told (lo, hi)
#R_EVENTS = 51                          ; events seen (written: the first 256 and the latest 256)
#R_PHIST = 64                           ; the period's histogram: words 64-127, 1 ms each, the last 63 ms and over
#R_WHIST = 128                          ; the work's histogram: words 128-191
#R_T = 192                              ; version 3: NesRecT(0 .. #NES_REC_T - 1) over the run, each 64 bits (lo, hi):
                                        ; words 192-211 (the #T_ list below)
#R_HASHES = 212                         ; version 4: picture hashes written (NesRecPicture)
#R_HASHSTOP = 213                       ; the guest frame at which a button was first seen (hashing stopped), 0 none yet
#R_SYNCLK = 214                         ; version 6 (N10, the synthesis on the RSP): its jobs' RSP clocks (DPC_CLOCK, lo, hi),
#R_SYNJOBS = 216                        ; its jobs, its renders for room (a log full), the samples it has rendered
#R_SYNROOMS = 217
#R_SYNDONE = 218
; an event's words (NesRecEvent)
#E_FRAME = 0                            ; the guest frame
#E_FLAGS = 1                            ; why: 1 an underrun, 2 a picture skipped, 4 work over one NES frame, 8 a drain,
                                        ; 16 a wait | underruns << 8 | pictures skipped << 16 | PPUMASK << 24
#E_WORK = 2                             ; the frame's work, Count ticks
#E_PERIOD = 3                           ; the frame's period, Count ticks
#E_SOUND = 4                            ; the sound buffer: samples made and not yet given to the AI (16 bits) | the AI's
                                        ; current DMA, samples left (AI_LEN / 4) << 16
#E_BANKS = 5                            ; CHR 1 KB slots switched | PRG slots switched << 8 | palette bytes changed << 16
                                        ; | PPUCTRL << 24 (each against the frame before)
#E_NT = 6                               ; name-table 64-byte blocks changed (of 64) | bands << 8 | drains << 16 | waits << 24
#E_MORE = 7                             ; fallback lines (12 bits) | tenths of a second since the first frame << 12
; version 3, the frame's work split (Count ticks; the #T_ list: what each part is and where it is counted)
#E_TBAND = 8                            ; band closes
#E_TFB = 9                              ; fallback lines drawn by the old renderer (the catch-up, the line's spans, its
                                        ; sprite row, its publish)
#E_TLIST = 10                           ; the fallback lines' list to the RDP (inside #E_TSHOW)
#E_TSHOW = 11                           ; the hand-over: the check points' polls, line 240's frame end, drains (their
                                        ; waits for the RSP, the RDP or a buffer included; the sleep for a buffer not)
#E_TAPU = 12                            ; the APU timing (u_apuadvance in the hot unit, all its calls)
#E_NAPU = 13                            ; APU timing calls (16 bits) | of them the segment path (a frame-sequencer
                                        ; step or a $4017 reset inside the interval) << 16
#E_NBUS = 14                            ; DMC bytes fetched (16 bits) | PPU bus writes ($2007) << 16
#E_NSPLIT = 15                          ; of the fallback lines: split lines (16 bits) | the others (priority-quirk
                                        ; candidates, lines of a band not recorded) << 16
#E_TSYN = 16                            ; version 5: the sound's synthesis (an AI block at a time, apusynth.n64)
#E_TREST = 17                           ; version 5: what is left of the work - the guest CPU, the PPU state machine and
                                        ; the bus (work less bands, fallback lines, hand-over, APU timing, synthesis)
; NesRecT: the parts, accumulated since the power-on (declared in show.n64, written by the timed code)
#T_BAND = 0
#T_FB = 1
#T_LIST = 2
#T_SHOW = 3
#T_APU = 4
#T_NAPU = 5                             ; counts from here
#T_NAPUSEG = 6
#T_NDMC = 7
#T_N2007 = 8
#T_SYN = 9
#NES_REC_T = 10
; THE SC64'S OWN REGISTERS (the hardware carts' RsScCmd / RsScEnable)
#NES_SC_ST = $BFFF0000
#NES_SC_D0 = $BFFF0004
#NES_SC_D1 = $BFFF0008
#NES_SC_IDR = $BFFF000C
#NES_SC_KEY = $BFFF0010
#NES_SC_ID = $53437632                  ; "SCv2"
#NES_SC_WAIT = 4687500                  ; 100 ms of Count

Global NesRecOn.i, NesRecBase.i, NesRecScD1.i
Global NesRecLast.i, NesRecLastWait.i, NesRecFirst.i
Global NesRecPSum.i, NesRecWSum.i, NesRecRspSeen.i, NesRecShownSeen.i, NesRecNotSeen.i, NesRecStarveSeen.i
Global NesRecWinP.i, NesRecWinW.i, NesRecWinHeld.i
; the frame before, for the events' "what changed in this frame"
Global NesRecBandsSeen.i, NesRecFbSeen.i, NesRecDrainSeen.i, NesRecWaitSeen.i, NesRecSkipSeen.i, NesRecStarveFrame.i
Global Dim NesRecChrLast.i(8)
Global Dim NesRecPrgLast.i(4)
Global Dim NesRecPalLast.a(32)
Global Dim NesRecNtSig.i(64)
Global Dim NesRecE.i(#NES_REC_EVENT_WORDS)   ; the event being written (NesRecEventCheck, NesRecEvent)
Global Dim NesRecTLast.i(#NES_REC_T)    ; NesRecT at the frame before's wrap (the frame's parts are the differences)
Global Dim NesRecTD.i(#NES_REC_T)       ; this frame's parts
Global NesRecSplitSeen.i
Global Dim NesRecDpcLast.i(4)
Global Dim NesRecDpcSum.i(4)
Global Dim NesRecW.i(#NES_REC_WORDS)    ; the summary as counted
Global Dim NesRecShadow.i(#NES_REC_WORDS) ; the summary as last written

; A command to the SC64: 1 done, 0 refused, -1 still busy after 100 ms; its DATA1 in NesRecScD1.
Procedure.i NesRecScCmd(cmd.i, d0.i, d1.i)
  Protected t.i, st.i
  LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_SC_D0, d0) : LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_SC_D1, d1)
  LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_SC_ST, cmd)
  t = LpmCpuCount()
  Repeat
    st = LpmDebugIoRead(#NES_SC_ST) & $FFFFFFFF
    If (st & $80000000) = 0 : Break : EndIf
    If ((LpmCpuCount() - t) & $FFFFFFFF) >= #NES_SC_WAIT : NesRecScD1 = -1 : ProcedureReturn -1 : EndIf
  ForEver
  NesRecScD1 = LpmDebugIoRead(#NES_SC_D1) & $FFFFFFFF
  If st & $40000000 : ProcedureReturn 0 : EndIf
  ProcedureReturn 1
EndProcedure

; The SC64 unlocked and its ROM space made writable (config 1, "ROM write enable"), as the NES tile probe and the
; neon-port carts do (their RsScEnable). WHETHER A WRITE LANDS IS DECIDED ONLY BY READING THE HEADER BACK
; (NesRecOpen), never by the value config 1 reads: on the owner's SC64 (firmware 2.20.2) it reads back 4 once set,
; not 1 (the tile probe's console log: "rom write was 0, now 4 (read 1, set 1, read back 1)"; run 69's listener
; left it at 4). The first console cart demanded 1 here, returned before writing anything and kept nothing - its
; dump was all zeros (2026-11-26). The project's emulator answers the identifier with $000C000C and keeps cartridge
; writes without being asked. Returns 1 always; the line printed says what the SC64 answered.
Procedure.i NesRecScEnable()
  Protected id.i, r.i
  LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_SC_KEY, 0)
  LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_SC_KEY, $5F554E4C)                ; "_UNL"
  LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_SC_KEY, $4F434B5F)                ; "OCK_"
  id = LpmDebugIoRead(#NES_SC_IDR) & $FFFFFFFF
  If id <> #NES_SC_ID
    LpmDebugPrint("NES RECORD: no SummerCart64 identifier ($" + Hex(id) + "): nothing switched, the write is tried")
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  r = NesRecScCmd($63, 1, 0)                             ; read config 1
  If r = 1 And NesRecScD1 = 0 : NesRecScCmd($43, 1, 1) : EndIf   ; set it
  r = NesRecScCmd($63, 1, 0)
  LpmDebugPrint("NES RECORD: SummerCart64, ROM write config reads " + Str(NesRecScD1) + " (command " + Str(r) + ")")
  ProcedureReturn 1
EndProcedure

; At start (RunGame, the display and the interrupts up): the header found or made, this power-on's slot cleared.
Procedure NesRecOpen()
  Protected crc.i, boots.i, slot.i, k.i
  NesRecOn = 0
  If NesRecScEnable() = 0 : ProcedureReturn : EndIf
  crc = LpmDebugIoRead($B0000010)
  If LpmDebugIoRead(#NES_REC) <> #NES_REC_MAGIC Or LpmDebugIoRead(#NES_REC + 4) <> crc Or LpmDebugIoRead(#NES_REC + 8) <> #NES_REC_VERSION
    LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_REC, 0)                         ; a fresh record (another ROM's or none): the magic last
    For k = 1 To 15 : LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_REC + k * 4, 0) : Next
    For k = 0 To #NES_REC_SLOTS - 1 : LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_REC + $1000 + k * #NES_REC_SLOT, 0) : Next   ; no old run
    LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_REC + 4, crc)
    LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_REC + 8, #NES_REC_VERSION)
    LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_REC, #NES_REC_MAGIC)
    If LpmDebugIoRead(#NES_REC) <> #NES_REC_MAGIC
      LpmDebugPrint("NES RECORD: the write to the flash cart did not land, nothing kept") : ProcedureReturn
    EndIf
  EndIf
  LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_REC + 20, #NES_REC_HASH_MAX)       ; version 5: the picture hashes' room and period, which
  LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_REC + 24, #NES_REC_HASH_EVERY)     ; size the run slots (the decoder reads them here)
  boots = LpmDebugIoRead(#NES_REC + 12) + 1
  slot = (boots - 1) % #NES_REC_SLOTS
  LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_REC + 12, boots)
  LpmDebugIoWrite(#NES_REC + 16, slot)
  NesRecBase = #NES_REC + $1000 + slot * #NES_REC_SLOT
  LpmDebugIoWrite(NesRecBase, 0)                         ; the slot not valid while it is cleared
  For k = 1 To #NES_REC_WORDS - 1
    LpmDebugIoWrite(NesRecBase + k * 4, 0) : NesRecW(k) = 0 : NesRecShadow(k) = 0
  Next
  NesRecW(#R_BOOT) = boots : NesRecW(#R_STATE) = 1
  LpmDebugIoWrite(NesRecBase + #R_BOOT * 4, boots) : NesRecShadow(#R_BOOT) = boots
  LpmDebugIoWrite(NesRecBase + #R_STATE * 4, 1) : NesRecShadow(#R_STATE) = 1
  LpmDebugIoWrite(NesRecBase, #NES_REC_RUN_MAGIC)
  NesRecOn = 1 : NesRecKept = 1         ; the side bands green (show.n64); yellow if this point is never reached
  LpmDebugPrint("NES RECORD: flash cart SDRAM $0" + Hex(#NES_REC - $B0000000) + ", power-on " + Str(boots) + ", slot " + Str(slot))
EndProcedure

; The summary out: every word that changed since it last went out, a PI write each.
Procedure NesRecPutAll()
  Protected k.i, v.i
  For k = 1 To #NES_REC_WORDS - 1
    v = NesRecW(k) & $FFFFFFFF
    If v <> NesRecShadow(k) : LpmDebugIoWrite(NesRecBase + k * 4, v) : NesRecShadow(k) = v : EndIf
  Next
EndProcedure

Procedure NesRecSplit(k.i, v.i)          ; a 64-bit count into words k (low) and k + 1 (high)
  NesRecW(k) = v & $FFFFFFFF : NesRecW(k + 1) = (v >> 32) & $FFFFFFFF
EndProcedure

; The counts the game keeps itself, copied into the summary; the window's series entry; the summary out.
Procedure NesRecFlush(frame.i, entry.i)
  Protected a.i, k.i, n.i, x.i
  NesRecW(#R_FRAMES) = frame
  NesRecW(#R_SHOWN) = NesShowStat(0) : NesRecW(#R_NOTWORDS) = NesShowStat(1) : NesRecW(#R_NOTSOUND) = NesShowStat(14)
  NesRecW(#R_OVER) = NesShowStat(2)
  NesRecW(#R_STARVE) = HostAiStarvations : NesRecW(#R_STARVELAST) = HostAiLastStarvation : NesRecW(#R_DROPPED) = HostAudioDropped
  NesRecSplit(#R_PSUM, NesRecPSum) : NesRecSplit(#R_WSUM, NesRecWSum)
  NesRecSplit(#R_RSPSUM, NesShowStat(12)) : NesRecW(#R_RSPMAX) = NesShowStat(13)
  For k = 0 To 3 : NesRecSplit(#R_DPC + 2 * k, NesRecDpcSum(k)) : Next
  NesRecW(#R_WAITS) = NesShowStat(3) : NesRecW(#R_DRAINS) = NesShowStat(4) : NesRecW(#R_FBLINES) = NesShowStat(5)
  NesRecW(#R_FBMOST) = NesShowStat(6) : NesRecW(#R_SPLIT) = NesShowStat(7) : NesRecW(#R_LOST) = NesShowStat(8)
  NesRecW(#R_BANDS) = NesShowStat(10) : NesRecW(#R_BANDMAX) = NesShowStat(11)
  NesRecSplit(#R_SLEEP, NesRecWait)
  For k = 0 To #NES_REC_T - 1 : NesRecSplit(#R_T + 2 * k, NesRecT(k)) : Next
  CompilerIf #NES_RSP_SYN
    NesRecSplit(#R_SYNCLK, NesSynClocks) : NesRecW(#R_SYNJOBS) = NesSynJobs : NesRecW(#R_SYNROOMS) = NesSynRooms
    NesRecW(#R_SYNDONE) = NesSynDone
  CompilerEndIf
  If entry And NesRecW(#R_ENTRIES) < #NES_REC_SERIES_MAX
    a = NesRecBase + #NES_REC_SERIES + NesRecW(#R_ENTRIES) * 16
    n = NesShowStat(0) - NesRecShownSeen : If n > 255 : n = 255 : EndIf
    x = n
    n = NesShowStat(1) + NesShowStat(14) - NesRecNotSeen : If n > 255 : n = 255 : EndIf
    x = x | (n << 8)
    n = HostAiStarvations - NesRecStarveSeen : If n > 255 : n = 255 : EndIf
    x = x | (n << 16) | ((NesRecWinHeld & 255) << 24)
    LpmDebugIoWrite(a, x)
    LpmDebugIoWrite(a + 4, NesRecWinP)
    LpmDebugIoWrite(a + 8, NesRecWinW)
    LpmDebugIoWrite(a + 12, (NesShowStat(12) - NesRecRspSeen) & $FFFFFFFF)
    NesRecW(#R_ENTRIES) + 1
  EndIf
  If entry
    NesRecShownSeen = NesShowStat(0) : NesRecNotSeen = NesShowStat(1) + NesShowStat(14)
    NesRecStarveSeen = HostAiStarvations : NesRecRspSeen = NesShowStat(12)
    NesRecWinP = 0 : NesRecWinW = 0 : NesRecWinHeld = 0
  EndIf
  NesRecW(#R_UPDATES) + 1
  NesRecPutAll()
EndProcedure

; What the game changed since the frame before, from state the port keeps anyway (no counter in the hot unit):
; the eight 1 KB CHR slots and the four PRG slots (MapChrSlots / MapPrgSlots: a bank switch), the 32 palette bytes,
; and the name tables as 64 blocks of 64 bytes, each folded to one word (rotate-xor of its 8 doublewords) and
; compared with the frame before's fold - a screen being redrawn (a world entered, a map shown) changes many blocks,
; a scrolling playfield a few. OUT: chr | prg << 8 | pal << 16 | nt << 24 (each 8 bits), the baselines moved on.
; Its cost: ~600 loads a frame, compiled code at the frame's wrap.
Procedure.i NesRecChanges()
  Protected k.i, j.i, x.i, v.i, nchr.i, nprg.i, npal.i, blocks.i, a.i
  For k = 0 To 7
    If MapChrSlots(k) <> NesRecChrLast(k) : nchr + 1 : NesRecChrLast(k) = MapChrSlots(k) : EndIf
  Next
  For k = 0 To 3
    If MapPrgSlots(k) <> NesRecPrgLast(k) : nprg + 1 : NesRecPrgLast(k) = MapPrgSlots(k) : EndIf
  Next
  For k = 0 To 31
    If Pal(k) <> NesRecPalLast(k) : npal + 1 : NesRecPalLast(k) = Pal(k) : EndIf
  Next
  a = @Nt(0)
  For k = 0 To 63
    x = 0
    For j = 0 To 7
      v = PeekQ(a) : a + 8
      x = ((x << 7) | ((x >> 57) & $7F)) ! v
    Next
    If x <> NesRecNtSig(k) : blocks + 1 : NesRecNtSig(k) = x : EndIf
  Next
  ProcedureReturn nchr | (nprg << 8) | (npal << 16) | (blocks << 24)
EndProcedure

; One event out (16 words, PI writes): entries 0-255 are the run's first events, 256-511 a ring of the latest.
Procedure NesRecEvent()          ; the event in NesRecE
  Protected n.i = NesRecW(#R_EVENTS), slot.i, a.i, k.i
  If n < 256 : slot = n : Else : slot = 256 + ((n - 256) & 255) : EndIf
  a = NesRecBase + #NES_REC_EVENTS + slot * #NES_REC_EVENT_WORDS * 4
  For k = 0 To #NES_REC_EVENT_WORDS - 1 : LpmDebugIoWrite(a + k * 4, NesRecE(k) & $FFFFFFFF) : Next
  NesRecW(#R_EVENTS) + 1
EndProcedure

; Every frame: an event when the frame had a sound underrun, a picture skipped, a drain or a wait, or its work
; exceeded one NES frame - with what the frame did (NesRecChanges) and the sound buffer at this moment.
Procedure.i NesRecSat16(v.i)            ; a count into 16 bits (65,535 and over: 65,535)
  If v < 0 : ProcedureReturn 0 : EndIf
  If v > $FFFF : ProcedureReturn $FFFF : EndIf
  ProcedureReturn v
EndProcedure

Procedure NesRecEventCheck(frame.i, d.i, w.i)
  Protected ch.i, starve.i, skip.i, bands.i, fb.i, drains.i, waits.i, why.i, q.i, ai.i, k.i, split.i
  For k = 0 To #NES_REC_T - 1 : NesRecTD(k) = NesRecT(k) - NesRecTLast(k) : NesRecTLast(k) = NesRecT(k) : Next
  split = NesShowStat(7) - NesRecSplitSeen : NesRecSplitSeen = NesShowStat(7)
  ch = NesRecChanges()
  starve = HostAiStarvations - NesRecStarveFrame : NesRecStarveFrame = HostAiStarvations
  skip = NesShowStat(1) + NesShowStat(14) - NesRecSkipSeen : NesRecSkipSeen = NesShowStat(1) + NesShowStat(14)
  bands = NesShowStat(10) - NesRecBandsSeen : NesRecBandsSeen = NesShowStat(10)
  fb = NesShowStat(5) - NesRecFbSeen : NesRecFbSeen = NesShowStat(5)
  drains = NesShowStat(4) - NesRecDrainSeen : NesRecDrainSeen = NesShowStat(4)
  waits = NesShowStat(3) - NesRecWaitSeen : NesRecWaitSeen = NesShowStat(3)
  If starve : why | 1 : EndIf
  If skip : why | 2 : EndIf
  If w > #NES_REC_SLOW : why | 4 : EndIf
  If drains : why | 8 : EndIf
  If waits : why | 16 : EndIf
  If why = 0 : ProcedureReturn : EndIf
  q = ApuProduced - HostPcmRead : If q < 0 : q = 0 : EndIf : If q > $FFFF : q = $FFFF : EndIf
  ai = (PeekL($A4500004) & $3FFFF) >> 2                  ; AI_LEN: bytes left of the DMA playing, as samples
  NesRecE(#E_FRAME) = frame
  NesRecE(#E_FLAGS) = why | ((starve & 255) << 8) | ((skip & 255) << 16) | ((PpuMask & 255) << 24)
  NesRecE(#E_WORK) = w : NesRecE(#E_PERIOD) = d
  NesRecE(#E_SOUND) = q | ((ai & $FFFF) << 16)
  NesRecE(#E_BANKS) = (ch & $FFFFFF) | ((PpuCtrl & 255) << 24)
  NesRecE(#E_NT) = ((ch >> 24) & 255) | ((bands & 255) << 8) | ((drains & 255) << 16) | ((waits & 255) << 24)
  q = NesRecPSum / 4687500 : If fb > 4095 : fb = 4095 : EndIf
  NesRecE(#E_MORE) = fb | ((q & $FFFFF) << 12)
  NesRecE(#E_TBAND) = NesRecTD(#T_BAND) : NesRecE(#E_TFB) = NesRecTD(#T_FB) : NesRecE(#E_TLIST) = NesRecTD(#T_LIST)
  NesRecE(#E_TSHOW) = NesRecTD(#T_SHOW) : NesRecE(#E_TAPU) = NesRecTD(#T_APU)
  NesRecE(#E_NAPU) = NesRecSat16(NesRecTD(#T_NAPU)) | (NesRecSat16(NesRecTD(#T_NAPUSEG)) << 16)
  NesRecE(#E_NBUS) = NesRecSat16(NesRecTD(#T_NDMC)) | (NesRecSat16(NesRecTD(#T_N2007)) << 16)
  NesRecE(#E_NSPLIT) = NesRecSat16(split) | (NesRecSat16(fb - split) << 16)
  NesRecE(#E_TSYN) = NesRecTD(#T_SYN)
  NesRecE(#E_TREST) = w - NesRecTD(#T_BAND) - NesRecTD(#T_FB) - NesRecTD(#T_SHOW) - NesRecTD(#T_APU) - NesRecTD(#T_SYN)
  NesRecEvent()
EndProcedure

; Once a guest frame, at its wrap (NesHostGuestFrame): the period since the last wrap, the work in it, the RDP's
; counters, the pads; every #NES_REC_WINDOW frames the summary and a series entry out.
Procedure NesRecFrame(frame.i)
  Protected now.i, d.i, w.i, ms.i, k.i, c.i, v.i
  If NesRecOn = 0 : ProcedureReturn : EndIf
  now = LpmCpuCount() & $FFFFFFFF
  If NesRecFirst = 0                                     ; the first guest frame: the readings to measure from
    NesRecFirst = 1
    NesRecW(#R_STATE) = 2
    For k = 0 To 3 : NesRecDpcLast(k) = PeekL($A4100010 + 4 * k) & $FFFFFF : Next
    NesRecChanges()                                      ; the baselines of "what changed in a frame"
    NesRecBandsSeen = NesShowStat(10) : NesRecFbSeen = NesShowStat(5) : NesRecDrainSeen = NesShowStat(4)
    NesRecWaitSeen = NesShowStat(3) : NesRecSkipSeen = NesShowStat(1) + NesShowStat(14) : NesRecStarveFrame = HostAiStarvations
    For k = 0 To #NES_REC_T - 1 : NesRecTLast(k) = NesRecT(k) : Next
    NesRecSplitSeen = NesShowStat(7)
  Else
    d = (now - NesRecLast) & $FFFFFFFF
    w = d - (NesRecWait - NesRecLastWait)
    If w < 0 : w = 0 : EndIf
    NesRecPSum + d : NesRecWSum + w : NesRecW(#R_MEASURED) + 1
    If d > NesRecW(#R_PMAX) : NesRecW(#R_PMAX) = d : NesRecW(#R_PMAXF) = frame : EndIf
    If w > NesRecW(#R_WMAX) : NesRecW(#R_WMAX) = w : NesRecW(#R_WMAXF) = frame : EndIf
    If d > NesRecWinP : NesRecWinP = d : EndIf
    If w > NesRecWinW : NesRecWinW = w : EndIf
    ms = d / #NES_REC_MS : If ms > 63 : ms = 63 : EndIf
    NesRecW(#R_PHIST + ms) + 1
    ms = w / #NES_REC_MS : If ms > 63 : ms = 63 : EndIf
    NesRecW(#R_WHIST + ms) + 1
    For k = 0 To 3
      c = PeekL($A4100010 + 4 * k) & $FFFFFF              ; DPC CLOCK, BUFBUSY, PIPEBUSY, TMEM
      v = (c - NesRecDpcLast(k)) & $FFFFFF
      NesRecDpcSum(k) + v : NesRecDpcLast(k) = c
      If k = 2 And v > NesRecW(#R_PIPEMAX) : NesRecW(#R_PIPEMAX) = v : EndIf
    Next
    NesRecEventCheck(frame, d, w)
  EndIf
  NesRecLast = now : NesRecLastWait = NesRecWait
  If (NesController | NesController2) <> 0 : NesRecW(#R_HELD) + 1 : NesRecWinHeld + 1 : EndIf
  NesRecW(#R_PADS) = (NesController & 255) | ((NesController2 & 255) << 8)
  If frame % #NES_REC_WINDOW = 0 : NesRecFlush(frame, 1) : EndIf
EndProcedure

; NesRecHashFb(fb) - the NES picture in a shown buffer (KSEG0, invalidated; 320 x 240 RGBA16, the NES at x 32-287)
; hashed in two parts, a doubleword (4 pixels) at a time, rotate-xor-add as the video digest and the show check
; (NesShowHashFb): per row, NES columns 0-239 (60 doublewords) into NesRecHashA, then columns 240-255 (4) into
; NesRecHashB. IN: a0 the buffer. CLOBBERS a0-a2, t0-t3, v0, v1.
Global NesRecHashA.i, NesRecHashB.i
ProcedureNaked NesRecHashFb(fb.i)
  ASM
    sll a0, a0, 0                    ; the address, sign-extended
    la t0, global_nesrechasha
    ld t3, 0(t0)                     ; t3 = hash A (columns 0-239)
    la t0, global_nesrechashb
    ld v1, 0(t0)                     ; v1 = hash B (columns 240-255)
    daddiu a0, a0, 64                ; x 32: NES column 0
    addiu a2, zero, 240              ; rows
nes_rec_hash_row:
    daddiu a1, a0, 480               ; the end of columns 0-239 (240 pixels x 2 bytes)
nes_rec_hash_a:
    ld t1, 0(a0)
    daddiu a0, a0, 8
    xor t3, t3, t1
    dsll t2, t3, 7
    dsrl32 t3, t3, 25
    or t3, t3, t2                    ; rotate left 7
    bne a0, a1, nes_rec_hash_a
    daddu t3, t3, t1                 ; (delay slot) + the doubleword
    daddiu a1, a0, 32                ; columns 240-255 (16 pixels)
nes_rec_hash_b:
    ld t1, 0(a0)
    daddiu a0, a0, 8
    xor v1, v1, t1
    dsll t2, v1, 7
    dsrl32 v1, v1, 25
    or v1, v1, t2
    bne a0, a1, nes_rec_hash_b
    daddu v1, v1, t1
    daddiu a0, a0, 128               ; the next row's x 32 (a row is 640 bytes)
    addiu a2, a2, -1
    bnez a2, nes_rec_hash_row
    nop
    la t0, global_nesrechasha
    sd t3, 0(t0)
    la t0, global_nesrechashb
    jr ra
    sd v1, 0(t0)
  EndASM
EndProcedure

; A frame's picture is drawn and shown (show.n64, NesShowFrameEnd: its SYNC_FULL waited, its buffer not yet given to
; another frame): hashed into the record while no button has been seen, one frame in #NES_REC_HASH_EVERY.
Procedure NesRecPicture(frame.i, fb.i, fbl.i)
  Protected n.i, a.i
  If NesRecOn = 0 Or NesRecW(#R_HASHSTOP) : ProcedureReturn : EndIf
  CompilerIf #NES_REC_HASH_PADSTOP
    If (NesController | NesController2) <> 0 : NesRecW(#R_HASHSTOP) = frame : ProcedureReturn : EndIf
  CompilerEndIf
  If fb = 0 Or frame % #NES_REC_HASH_EVERY : ProcedureReturn : EndIf
  n = NesRecW(#R_HASHES)
  If n >= #NES_REC_HASH_MAX : ProcedureReturn : EndIf
  Protected t0.i = LpmCpuCount()
  fb = (fb & $1FFFFFFF) | $80000000
  LpmCacheInvalidateData(fb, #HOST_WIDTH * #HOST_HEIGHT * 2)
  NesRecHashA = $351B5058 : NesRecHashB = $351B5058
  NesRecHashFb(fb)
  a = NesRecBase + #NES_REC_HASHES + n * 32
  LpmDebugIoWrite(a, frame)
  LpmDebugIoWrite(a + 4, NesRecHashA & $FFFFFFFF) : LpmDebugIoWrite(a + 8, (NesRecHashA >> 32) & $FFFFFFFF)
  LpmDebugIoWrite(a + 12, NesRecHashB & $FFFFFFFF) : LpmDebugIoWrite(a + 16, (NesRecHashB >> 32) & $FFFFFFFF)
  LpmDebugIoWrite(a + 20, fbl)
  NesRecW(#R_HASHES) = n + 1
  NesRecT(3) - ((LpmCpuCount() - t0) & $FFFFFFFF)   ; the hash is the record's own, not the hand-over's (it runs
EndProcedure                                       ; inside NesShowFrameEnd, which is timed as the hand-over)

; The emulator stopped (RunGame's NES STOP): its reason, and the whole summary out now.
Procedure NesRecStop()
  If NesRecOn = 0 : ProcedureReturn : EndIf
  NesRecW(#R_STATE) = 3 : NesRecW(#R_CODE) = BadOpcode : NesRecW(#R_PC) = PC : NesRecW(#R_WORKER) = WorkerError
  NesRecFlush(WorkerFrames, 0)
EndProcedure

; The game did not start (2: the cartridge did not load, 3: the show's set-up refused).
Procedure NesRecRefused(code.i)
  If NesRecOn = 0 : ProcedureReturn : EndIf
  NesRecW(#R_STATE) = 4 : NesRecW(#R_CODE) = code
  NesRecPutAll()
EndProcedure
